        <div id="which-to-buy" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            10. Which 12V Fridge Should You Buy?
          </h2>

          <p>
            If you camp often, overland, or want one fridge to last many years, buy the <strong>Dometic CFX3 45</strong>. It is the most refined single-zone fridge here, efficient enough to run comfortably from a 1kWh power station or a dual-battery setup, and built to survive years of vehicle life. If the Dometic price is hard to justify, the <strong>ICECO VL45</strong> gives you a well-known compressor and a tougher metal body for meaningfully less, with only the controls and app feeling less polished.
          </p>

          <p>
            Couples and solo campers on a budget should look at the <strong>BougeRV 30 Quart</strong>, which gets you real compressor cooling and freezer capability in a box that fits behind a seat. If you mostly need a drinks and lunch cooler, a cab fridge for a work truck, or a second fridge for beverages, the <strong>Alpicool C20</strong> is the least expensive way to get a compressor and the efficient choice for small power stations.
          </p>

          <p>
            Families on trips longer than a long weekend, or anyone who needs a freezer, should choose the <strong>Dometic CFX3 75DZ</strong>, as long as the vehicle has space and the power system has capacity for two zones. If you camp away from the car and want the fridge to run on its own battery, with ice at camp as a bonus, the <strong>EcoFlow Glacier</strong> is the most self-contained option here, at the cost of weight and complexity.
          </p>

          <p>
            And the <strong>Coleman PowerChill 40</strong>? Buy it only if you need a quiet drink cooler for day drives with the engine running. For camping it cannot keep food safe in summer heat, and the Alpicool costs only somewhat more. Whatever you choose, pair it with the right battery. Our <a href="/best-portable-power-station-for-camping/">camping power station guide</a> sizes the battery to the trip, and the <a href="/best-portable-power-station/">main power station roundup</a> covers bigger units if the fridge is one load among many.
          </p>
