          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most campers the answer is a compressor fridge, sized to the group and run from a power station or a dedicated battery rather than the starter battery. The Dometic CFX3 45 is the one to buy once; the ICECO VL45 is the value alternative; the BougeRV and Alpicool get you into compressor cooling for not much more than a thermoelectric box.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Pre-chill at home, keep the vents clear, set the right battery protection level, and plan on roughly 200W of solar if you want to stay out indefinitely. Do that and the ice runs end for good.
          </p>
